Code from doubletake
--------------------

The AirPlay protocol implementation in internal/airplay and the test receiver
in cmd/winairplay-test-receiver come from doubletake:

    https://github.com/omarroth/doubletake
    commit 5e2f1cbe3e1070bcefec8e549c7baf884727bc00 (2026-10-04)
    License: LGPL-3.0-or-later

This includes pairing (SRP-6a, pair-verify), the FairPlay SAP handshake, the
RTSP session, the mirror stream, the event channel and the test receiver.

Changes made for winairplay (2026-11-15):

  - The Go import path changed to github.com/bsdrip/winairplay.
  - internal/airplay/capture.go: the Linux process attribute moved to
    childproc_linux.go; FFmpeg capture is selected on Windows; the encoder
    names qsv, amf and mf are accepted; CaptureConfig has a Display field.
  - internal/airplay/credentials.go: the default credential file is in the
    winairplay directory of the user's configuration directory.
  - internal/airplay/credentials_keyring.go: the keyring service name is
    "winairplay".
  - internal/airplay/pairing.go: the default client name is
    "winairplay device".
  - cmd/winairplay-test-receiver: program name and environment variable name.
  - The doubletake daemon, the command line program, the KDE widget and the
    manual pages are not included.

New files in winairplay (not from doubletake):

  - internal/airplay/capture_ffmpeg.go (FFmpeg capture, H.264 and HEVC),
    audio_pcm.go, audio_platform.go, audio_loopback_windows.go,
    audio_loopback_other.go (sound capture), childproc_*.go, and their tests
  - internal/mirror (the session flow follows cmd/doubletake/main.go)
  - cmd/winairplay (tray application), installer, .github

internal/airplay/audio.go was changed to start the sound capture of
winairplay when FFmpeg capture is in use.

FFmpeg
------

The installer includes ffmpeg.exe, an unchanged build of FFmpeg from
https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/ (https://github.com/GyanD/codexffmpeg).
That build is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3. Its
license text is installed as FFMPEG-LICENSE.txt. The FFmpeg source code is
at https://ffmpeg.org. winairplay starts FFmpeg as a separate program.

